wo years.\nNOTE 5 - RELATIONSHIP WITH DUPONT Prior to the Separation, Qnity had been managed and operated in the normal course with other businesses of DuPont. Accordingly, certain shared costs had been allocated to Qnity and reflected as expenses in the stand-alone Consolidated Financial Statements. Management considers the allocation methodologies used to be reasonable and appropriate reflections of the pre-Separation expenses attributable to Qnity for purposes of the stand-alone financial statements. The expenses reflected in the Consolidated Financial Statements may not be indicative of expenses that will be incurred by Qnity in the future. All transactions with DuPont prior to the Separation approximate prices at cost.\n"}
